# The bundled font set of the PDF export (plan 32, DBR15b): Noto Sans, Noto Serif and Noto Sans Mono as WOFF2, regular (400) and bold (700), with the italics
# where upstream has them (Noto Sans Mono has no italic: the browser slants the regular when asked, and the plan does not promise more).
# Read by scripts/fetch-fonts.sh and scripts/fetch-fonts.ps1 (KEY=value lines, nothing else is evaluated). Fonts are the same on every platform: no rid entries.
# Each archive is checked against the SHA-256 recorded here, and so is every file taken from it (FILE= lines); the licence text of each family is checked and
# installed beside its files. Installed under .fonts/<family>/ (gitignored: the files are fetched at build or install time, never at run time, never committed).
#
# SOURCE. The npm packages @fontsource/noto-sans, -noto-serif and -noto-sans-mono 5.3.0 (https://github.com/fontsource/font-files, directory fonts/google/<family>),
# fetched from https://registry.npmjs.org (an immutable, versioned tarball URL; each archive's SHA-256 below was computed from the download and its sha512 matched
# the registry's recorded integrity). Why this source: it publishes WOFF2 already, one file per Unicode subset (the browser loads only the subsets a document uses,
# through unicode-range), whereas the notofonts GitHub releases (https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic/releases) are blocked from the authoring sandbox,
# publish TTF and OTF only, and would need a WOFF2 conversion step (fonttools, pinned) to be reproducible. The files are Google Fonts' build of Noto
# (static 400 and 700 instances of the variable NotoSans/NotoSerif[wdth,wght] fonts, subsetted and converted to WOFF2 by Fontsource); the upstream design is the
# Noto Project's (https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic). The unicode-range of each subset is in the package's 400.css, 700.css, 400-italic.css and
# 700-italic.css (the later slice that writes the @font-face block takes it from there). Subsets taken: latin, latin-ext, greek, greek-ext, cyrillic,
# cyrillic-ext, vietnamese. Not in the set: CJK, Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari and the other scripts (documented, not promised).
#
# LICENCE CHECK (done on the packages' own LICENSE files, which are the OFL.txt of the font project): every family is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
# ("This Font Software is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1"), npm metadata license OFL-1.1.
#   - Copyright line: "Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors (https://github.com/notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic)" (Noto Sans and Noto Serif add the same line for their italic
#     source file); none of the three declares a Reserved Font Name (the copyright line has no "with Reserved Font Name" clause), so the OFL's condition 3
#     (no use of a Reserved Font Name by a Modified Version) binds nothing; the aliases DbDataKit Sans, DbDataKit Serif and DbDataKit Mono are used regardless.
#   - Subsetting and WOFF2 conversion are allowed: the licence grants the right to "use, study, copy, merge, embed, modify, redistribute, and sell modified and unmodified
#     copies", and defines a Modified Version as including "changing formats". Condition 1: the fonts are never sold by themselves. Condition 2: bundled with software is
#     allowed "provided that each copy contains the above copyright notice and this license", which is why the licence text is installed next to the files (OFL.txt) and kept in
#     the repository under licenses/fonts/ (the installed export component must carry it too: DBR16). Condition 4: the Noto Project's and its authors' names are not used to promote the product.
#   - Condition 5: the Font Software stays under the OFL (the product's licence does not change it); the requirement does not apply to a document made with the fonts, so a PDF that embeds them is not affected.
# To move to new files: set VERSION (and the archive paths), then each archive's SHA-256, the licence's and every FILE's, and run scripts/fetch-fonts.sh. A font update re-pins this
# file only (never chromium.pin) and regenerates the exporter's goldens in the same change.
VERSION=5.3.0
BASE=https://registry.npmjs.org/@fontsource
FAMILIES=noto-sans noto-serif noto-sans-mono


